BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Dubrovnik//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Dubrovnik — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mali Ston oysters — The European flat oyster\, raw with lemon\, from the brackish bay where it grows.
DESCRIPTION:Say: MAH-lee ston ka-MEN-ee-tseh. Farmed in the bay since Roman times\, and protected by an EU designation since 2020. Best: Bota Šare\, Mali Ston — at the bay\, an hour north\; call for winter hours
LOCATION:Bota Šare\, Mali Ston — at the bay\, an hour north\; call for winter hours
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bota+Sare+Mali+Ston+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Šporki makaruli — Hand-cut macaroni under a slow beef ragù with bay and cloves.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SHPOR-kee ma-ka-ROO-lee. The city’s own pasta\, eaten above all in the week of St Blaise. Best: Kopun\, Poljana Ruđera Boškovića\, Old Town
LOCATION:Kopun\, Poljana Ruđera Boškovića\, Old Town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kopun+Poljana+Rudera+Boskovica+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Crni rižot — Risotto made black with cuttlefish and its ink.
DESCRIPTION:Say: TSUR-nee REE-zhot. The Adriatic’s own black rice\, which Dalmatia insists is no copy of Venice. Best: Proto\, Široka\, Old Town — open all year
LOCATION:Proto\, Široka\, Old Town — open all year
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Proto+Fish+Restaurant+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Janjetina ispod peke — Lamb and potatoes cooked for hours under an iron bell in the embers.
DESCRIPTION:Say: YAN-yeh-tee-na EES-pod PEH-keh. Cooked to your arrival\, so it has to be ordered hours ahead. Best: Konoba Dubrava\, Bosanka — order ahead\, and call to check it is open
LOCATION:Konoba Dubrava\, Bosanka — order ahead\, and call to check it is open
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Konoba+Dubrava+Bosanka+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pašticada — Beef braised for hours in wine and dried fruit\, with gnocchi.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pash-tee-TSA-da. A two-day dish of the whole Dalmatian coast\; ask before you count on it. Best: The konobas of the coast — ask a day ahead\; Konoba Konavoski Dvori\, Ljuta\, for the country table
LOCATION:The konobas of the coast — ask a day ahead\; Konoba Konavoski Dvori\, Ljuta\, for the country table
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Konoba+Konavoski+Dvori+Ljuta+Konavle+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ćevapi — Grilled minced-meat fingers in lepinja bread\, with raw onion and ajvar.
DESCRIPTION:Say: CHEH-va-pee. The Bosnian grill inside the walls holds a MICHELIN Bib Gourmand. Best: Taj Mahal\, Nikole Gučetića\, Old Town
LOCATION:Taj Mahal\, Nikole Gučetića\, Old Town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Taj+Mahal+Nikole+Gucetica+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pršut sandwich — Dalmatian air-dried ham and cheese in the house bread.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PUR-shoot. The cheapest good lunch inside the walls\, eaten standing. Best: Buffet Škola\, Antuninska\, Old Town
LOCATION:Buffet Škola\, Antuninska\, Old Town
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Buffet+Skola+Antuninska+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arancini — Candied bitter-orange peel rolled in sugar — not rice balls.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-ran-CHEE-nee. The city’s confection\, made from the part of the orange others throw away. Best: Kopun\, Old Town\, where they come with the coffee\; or the Gundulić Square stalls in the morning
LOCATION:Kopun\, Old Town\, where they come with the coffee\; or the Gundulić Square stalls in the morning
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kopun+Poljana+Rudera+Boskovica+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Rožata — The city’s caramel custard\, scented with rose liqueur.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ro-ZHA-ta. Dubrovnik’s own dessert\; the Rozalin in it is what makes it so. Best: The old houses of the Old Town\; ask at Proto
LOCATION:The old houses of the Old Town\; ask at Proto
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Proto+Fish+Restaurant+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Stonska torta — A cake of macaroni\, walnuts\, chocolate and cinnamon in shortcrust.
DESCRIPTION:Say: STON-ska TOR-ta. Ston’s strangest sweet\, tied by tradition to the building of its walls. Best: Ston and Mali Ston — ask at Bota Šare
LOCATION:Ston and Mali Ston — ask at Bota Šare
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bota+Sare+Mali+Ston+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Plavac Mali — The native red of Dalmatia\, dark and warm\, from the Pelješac slopes.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PLA-vats MA-lee. A close relative of California’s Zinfandel\; taste it at the cellar door. Best: Grgić Vina\, Trstenik\, Pelješac — call ahead
LOCATION:Grgić Vina\, Trstenik\, Pelješac — call ahead
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Grgic+Vina+Trstenik+Peljesac+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Dingač — Plavac Mali from the steepest south slope of Pelješac.
DESCRIPTION:Say: DEEN-gach. Croatia’s first protected wine\, 1961. Best: Vinarija Miloš\, Ponikve\, Pelješac — by appointment
LOCATION:Vinarija Miloš\, Ponikve\, Pelješac — by appointment
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Vinarija+Milos+Ponikve+Ston+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pošip — The white of Korčula: citrus\, salt and almond.
DESCRIPTION:Say: POH-ship. The glass the oysters want. Best: D'vino Wine Bar\, Palmotićeva\, Old Town — in season
LOCATION:D'vino Wine Bar\, Palmotićeva\, Old Town — in season
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=D%27vino+Wine+Bar+Dubrovnik+Croatia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:dubrovnik-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Travarica — Grape rakija steeped with herbs\, poured small before the meal.
DESCRIPTION:Say: tra-VA-ree-tsa. The truest Dalmatian opening gesture. Best: Any konoba of the coast\; Konoba Konavoski Dvori pours its own country rakija
LOCATION:Any konoba of the coast\; Konoba Konavoski Dvori pours its own country rakija
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Konoba+Konavoski+Dvori+Ljuta+Konavle+Croatia
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
